from pathlib import Path
import html
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
# Keep the required notice with both distributable forms of the game.
license_bytes=(root/'LICENSE').read_bytes()
(root/'game/LICENSE').write_bytes(license_bytes)
(root/'dist/LICENSE').write_bytes(license_bytes)
body='''<header><p>UZHHOROD · THE RIVER REMEMBERS</p><h1>The stories behind<br>the lights.</h1><p>A small reading room for the history in the game.</p><a href="./">← Return to the game</a></header><main>
<section><b>01 · THE CASTLE</b><h2>From fortress to museum</h2><p>The game uses the palace entrance date of 1598, the Union of Uzhhorod in 1646, and the museum’s move into the castle in 1947.</p><a href="https://www.zkmuseum.com/p/uzhhorod-castle-history.html">Read the castle museum’s history ↗</a></section>
<section><b>02 · THE SYNAGOGUE</b><h2>A community behind a facade</h2><p>The synagogue opened in 1904. Municipal tourism dates the philharmonic’s residence in the building to 1957; an organ was installed in 1974.</p><p>The Jewish community’s deportation and destruction in the Holocaust is remembered separately from the restoration puzzle.</p><a href="https://travel.rada-uzhgorod.gov.ua/?p=622">Municipal history of the synagogue ↗</a><a href="https://travel.rada-uzhgorod.gov.ua/?p=1674">Organ and architectural details ↗</a><a href="https://encyclopedia.yivo.org/article.aspx/Uzhhorod">YIVO: the Jewish history of Uzhhorod ↗</a><a href="https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/selections-of-jews-upon-arrival-at-auschwitz">USHMM: testimony of Anna Lax Patipa, including Ungvár ghetto ↗</a></section>
<section><b>03 · THE LIVING PROMENADE</b><h2>A garden for the next generation</h2><p>Municipal tourism dates the linden avenue to 1928. Visit Uzhhorod describes ornamental cherry trees arriving from Vienna in 1923. The game distinguishes the two plantings, and uses the seasonal cycle for this puzzle.</p><a href="https://travel.rada-uzhgorod.gov.ua/?p=636">The linden promenade ↗</a><a href="https://visit-uzhhorod.itc.gov.ua/2022/11/17/strong-do-uzhgoroda-na-sakury-strong/">Visit Uzhhorod: ornamental cherry trees ↗</a></section>
<section><b>04 · THE CROSSING</b><h2>The route survives the bridge</h2><p>The earlier iron bridge opened in 1898. The final toll disappeared in 1907, and the first city bus crossed in 1921. The bridge was destroyed in 1944; the modern footbridge is a later structure.</p><a href="https://travel.rada-uzhgorod.gov.ua/?p=640">Municipal history of the crossing ↗</a></section>
<section><b>05 · THE HERITAGE WALK</b><h2>Timber, towers and changing roles</h2><p>The Shelestovo Church of Archangel Michael is dated 1777. The museum records its move to Mukachevo in 1927 and its installation in Uzhhorod in 1974. The regional council describes oak beams, wooden shingles and a three-tower silhouette.</p><a href="https://www.uzhhorod-skansen.com/en/%D0%B4%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%88%D0%B5-%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE-%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D1%86%D1%96%D1%8E">The museum’s exhibition guide ↗</a><a href="https://zakarpat-rada.gov.ua/catalog/zakarpatskyj-muzej-narodnoyi-arhitektury-ta-pobutu/">Regional council: museum and church ↗</a><p>Municipal tourism dates the beginning of Holy Cross Cathedral’s construction to 1640, and the former Jesuit complex’s transfer to the Greek Catholic eparchy to 1775.</p><a href="https://travel.rada-uzhgorod.gov.ua/?p=599">Municipal history of Holy Cross Cathedral ↗</a></section><section><b>ARTISTIC INTERPRETATION</b><h2>An imagined city. Real histories.</h2><p>The miniature compresses geography and stylizes architecture. It does not reconstruct a single year. Glowing memories, the restoration mechanisms, six found objects, residents and their requests, the unsent letter, lantern-weaving, courier letters, town-day activities, the riverside workshop, Evening Company walks, the Little Exhibition and the river gathering are fictional. Exhibition objects are invented game objects, player keepsakes or authored source summaries; the pavilion, briefs, visitor notes and display replicas are not historical exhibits. The walk’s guests, dialogue, comfort measures and planning minutes are authored game systems, not historical testimony or real tour durations. Workshop boats use stylized game physics; the floating-light procession is an invented ritual, not a claim about a local historical custom. Archive cards are authored paraphrases of the linked sources, not facsimiles of original documents; their reading stations and the keeper’s account are invented. The accelerated clock and event times are game rules, not real opening hours. Four stories cannot encompass the whole city.</p><a href="https://wiki.starhermit.com/docs/tutorials/starhermit-engine.html">Built with StarHermit Engine 1.38.0 ↗</a></section></main>'''
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#102832;color:#f7ead1;font:17px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}header,main{max-width:1000px;margin:auto;padding:60px 28px}header p:first-child,b{font:11px/1.6 system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#e7bd7c}h1{font:clamp(42px,7vw,76px)/1.08 Georgia,serif;margin:25px 0}h2{font:31px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:17px 0}main{padding-top:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:30px}section{border-top:1px solid #4b686e;padding:28px 0}section:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}p{color:#b9ced0}a{display:block;color:#e7bd7c;text-underline-offset:5px;margin:12px 0;font-size:14px}a:hover{color:white}@media(max-width:650px){main{display:block}header{padding-top:40px}}'''
(root/'dist/sources.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Uzhhorod · Historical sources</title><style>'+css+'</style>'+body+'</html>')
# A normal page link keeps research accessible outside StarHermit’s platform-approved in-game links.
p=root/'dist/index.html';s=p.read_text()
if 'aria-label="Historical sources"' not in s:
    s=s.replace('</body>','<a href="sources.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Historical sources" style="position:fixed;bottom:9px;right:12px;z-index:2;color:#b9ced0;font:11px system-ui;text-decoration:none">Sources ↗</a>\n</body>')
p.write_text(s)

import hashlib,json
dist=root/'dist'
index={'format':1,'files':{str(p.relative_to(dist)):{'size':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for p in sorted(dist.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and p.name!='starhermit-files.json'}}
(dist/'starhermit-files.json').write_text(json.dumps(index,indent=2)+'\n')
